widgets, how many cartons are required?',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','89053375-542c-4c33-ac7d-3c0ad60dc612','set5'),(538,1,'SPEAKING_PROMPT','What do you think the people in this office are discussing, and how does teamwork help in a workplace like this?\r\nHave you ever worked or studied in a group environment similar to this? Describe your experience and the challenges you faced.\r\nWhat skills are important for employees to communicate effectively and maintain a positive office atmosphere?',NULL,'uploads/questions/q-cec5d881-4aae-4dbe-bd24-f29f57a79613.jpg',10,0,45,'click','null','c77eead6-c8c6-4bda-b1d4-89392233e7b9','set4'),(539,6,'WRITING_PROMPT','A company operational budget line is $10,000. It allocates 35% to infrastructure upgrade assets and 20% to software licensing subscriptions. How much budget remains unspent?',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','501fca10-96e5-4bdb-a078-0b85deda109c','set5'),(540,6,'MCQ','An express staff shuttle departs the main depot every 40 minutes. If the first shuttle leaves exactly at 07:00 AM, at what time does the fifth shuttle depart?',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','61f560e0-1946-4a03-99a3-453e55a02b74','set5'),(541,6,'WRITING_PROMPT','A remote fuel tank holds 750 liters of diesel. If a small valve leaks at a constant rate of 12 liters per hour, how many liters remain after 8 hours?',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','54653932-d27f-471e-87c9-46ca9e0888fb','set5'),(542,1,'SPEAKING_PROMPT','What do you think makes birthday celebrations special for families and friends?\r\nDescribe a memorable birthday party you have attended or celebrated. What made it enjoyable and unforgettable?\r\nHow do decorations, music, and activities create a happy atmosphere at events like this?',NULL,NULL,10,0,45,'click','null','4b10d51e-69f0-4a00-9184-175c084f08ac','set3'),(543,6,'MCQ','An auditorium layout is designed with 19 rows of chairs. If each row contains exactly 15 seats, find the maximum seating capacity of the room.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','39b837f7-a7c3-4c2e-8a35-41c0f9badef7','set5'),(544,6,'WRITING_PROMPT','A technician runs a performance diagnostic cycle on a server. The temperature drops from 15°C down to -10°C. Find the total temperature variance.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','7bc9faa7-565a-4130-9b44-424dec482621','set5'),(545,6,'WRITING_PROMPT','A commercial printing system yields 85 pages per minute. How many total pages are generated during a continuous run of 84 minutes?',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','5d8d5fc7-cbeb-4ab5-9128-d03d9a9d91bc','set5'),(546,6,'MCQ','Solve for the unknown value variable X in the workplace resource balancing expression: 7X - 17 = 270',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','50dee293-dd6b-4af8-adcf-f9c76c749085','set5'),(547,1,'SPEAKING_PROMPT','Why is community service and volunteering important for society and the environment?\r\nHave you ever participated in an outdoor activity like planting trees or cleaning public places? Describe your experience.\r\nHow can teamwork and cooperation help people complete activities like this more effectively?',NULL,'uploads/questions/q-15088d0c-67ca-4805-86ad-f58a2cf376e4.jpg',10,0,45,'click','null','24863ea0-0da0-4330-b304-6b98615dd13c','set2'),(548,1,'SPEAKING_PROMPT','What are the advantages and disadvantages of living in a large modern city like this?\r\nHow do transportation systems such as highways and flyovers help people in busy urban areas?\r\nDo you think cities in the future will become more crowded and technologically advanced? Explain your opinion.',NULL,'uploads/questions/q-2e5ed42f-962a-4b8c-be75-49074c2a5b8f.jpg',10,0,45,'click','null','bc6fb7a1-15e8-4aa2-a37d-3ce930f8fdbb','set1'),(549,6,'MCQ','A facilities supervisor tracks an equipment component failure rate of exactly 3%. If the warehouse handles 35000 components, how many failed units are expected?',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','640d1c5e-5fda-46ed-a388-7dc299742435','set5'),(550,6,'WRITING_PROMPT','A driver covers a distance of 630 km at an average speed of 60 km/h. How many total minutes did the trip take?',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','698c1663-2173-46f5-a3c1-af9d5b71adcb','set5'),(551,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Brian planned to see his friend tonight. Why does he say he can’t come?\r\nBrian said he can’t come because he is ____________ ','Brian: Hey, I\'m really sorry, but I won\'t be able to make it tonight. I know we planned to hang out, and I\'m not away on holiday or anything like that. I actually felt fine this morning, but I\'ve come down with a terrible headache and a fever this afternoon. I think it\'s best if I just stay in bed.',NULL,2,0,NULL,'click','null','c80ca4e1-79c5-4c45-aefb-4aac7f568686','set2'),(552,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Ken calls to plan a visit. When does Ken want his friend to visit?\r\nKen wants his friend to visit ______ \r\n','Ken: Hi there! I’m looking forward to coming over tonight. I know you said you’d be free from 7:30 onwards, but my meeting finished early. Would it be okay if I dropped by around 7:00 instead? Let me know if arriving before 7:30 works for you, otherwise I can just wait in a coffee shop nearby.',NULL,2,0,NULL,'click','null','0b84bae0-7588-46b6-8a2c-23fe5bdcabbe','set2'),(553,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Alan calls his friend to suggest ways of travelling to his city. How do most people get there?\r\nMost people travel to Alan\'s city by taking a _____________.\r\n','Alan: Hi! Just calling about your trip here next weekend. You could look into flights, but the airport is quite far out and planes are expensive. There is also a direct bus, but it takes ages. Honestly, the vast majority of visitors just take the train. The station is right in the city centre, so that\'s how most people choose to get here.',NULL,2,0,NULL,'click','null','404dc724-0a6b-454a-8697-a39eb4479896','set2'),(554,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Monica leaves you a message about her son Mark. What does he eat every morning?\r\nIn the morning, Mark usually has__________.\r\n','Monica: Hi, it\'s Monica. Thanks again for looking after Mark tomorrow morning. Just a quick note about his breakfast—he loves fish, but obviously not for breakfast! He usually refuses to drink his milk unless it\'s in hot chocolate, so please don\'t just give him a glass of it. Instead, he always expects scrambled or boiled eggs. He won\'t start his day without them!',NULL,2,0,NULL,'click','null','73070ccb-2d78-4c31-bf54-687f351ef8cc','set2'),(555,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Ana calls you to change when her party is. What day will the party be?\nAna\'s party next week will be on______________.\n','Ana: Hey! Look, regarding my party next week—I originally planned it for Friday night, but a lot of my family can only make it on Thursday. I thought about moving it to Saturday so everyone has the weekend, but the venue is fully booked then. So, we are going ahead with Thursday instead. Hope you can still make it!',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','f3a8ed2b-c6f2-43ef-b7b9-c4979899d406','set2'),(556,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Martin leaves his friend Maggie a message after a party. What did he lose?\nMartin lost his_____________','Martin: Hi Maggie, it\'s Martin. I had a great time at your party last night, thanks! Hey, I\'ve just realised I\'m missing something. Luckily, I still have my wallet with all my money, and my bag is right here on the floor. But I can\'t seem to find my glasses anywhere, and I can\'t read my book without them. Did I leave them at your house?',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','bada2134-3953-4777-a3d0-1c7667811c5e','set2'),(557,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to two friends discussing their plans. What do they decide to do?\nThe friends are going to______________.\n','Friend A: The weather is beautiful today. Should we go for a walk in the woods?\nFriend B: Oh, we did that last weekend. What about heading to the outdoor pool for a swim?\nFriend A: It might be a bit crowded today. Why don’t we just pack some sandwiches and sit on the grass at the local park?\nFriend B: Yeah, actually, that sounds really relaxing. Let\'s do that instead.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','c53f6c86-04de-4269-b63f-aa8bc6f684e6','set2'),(558,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a woman in a shop. What type of TV does she want to buy?\r\nThe woman wants to buy ____________.\r\n','Customer: Hello, I’m looking for a new television. I definitely don\'t want one of those bulky, old-fashioned TVs that take up half the living room. I know the salesman tried to show me a top-of-the-range model, but I\'m on a budget and can\'t afford an expensive TV. I just want a basic, modern flat screen TV that I can mount on my wall.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','a948fc03-7379-4380-ad54-b56d973b6af6','set2'),(559,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a person talking about a house. What doesn\'t she like about it?\nShe is going to remove the -------------.\n','Speaker: The new house is lovely. The windows are huge and let in so much natural light, and the old wooden doors have so much character that I\'m definitely keeping them. However, the previous owners put down this horrible, dark green carpet in the living room. It makes the whole space look tiny and dated, so I\'m going to rip it out next week.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','5ec784b5-64d1-47c6-a6d8-8fad0a17d6a2','set2'),(560,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to the radio announcement. Whose birthday is it in May?\nThe person who has a birthday in May is _________.\n','Presenter: Time for our monthly shout-outs! First up, a big happy birthday to Kitty, who celebrated her special day back in March. Next month, in June, Paul will be turning sixteen. But today, we want to send our best wishes to George, who is celebrating his birthday this week, right here in the middle of May! Have a great day, George!',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','1b968ec1-7a4d-41a0-bc0d-5a3079111602','set2'),(561,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Alana calls her colleague. What time is the car getting her?\nThe car is coming at _____________.\n','Alana: Hi Sarah, just updating you on my travel arrangements for the conference. The company originally booked the taxi to pick me up at 12:30 pm, but I realised I wouldn\'t have enough time to pack my files. I asked them to delay it until 2:30 pm, but that was too late. In the end, we compromised and scheduled the car for 12:45 pm exactly.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','fea1d4cd-8854-43c5-9740-21ac8103a90f','set2'),(562,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Two friends are talking about a job. Why is the job difficult?\nThe difficult thing about the job is working\n','Friend A: How are you finding the new job at the hospital?\nFriend B: It\'s tough. The people are great—I thought working with doctors might be intimidating, but they are all incredibly supportive. The schedule isn\'t too bad either, as I get to have my weekends off. The real issue is the sheer length of the shifts. Working twelve-hour long hours every day is just exhausting.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','a7b3e93a-8518-48f5-a6fc-b7cc43c51358','set2'),(563,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to an announcement in a department store. Which items have the best reductions this weekend?\nThis weekend, the best reductions are on __________________.\n','Announcer: Attention shoppers! Welcome to our weekend clearance event. We have great deals across the store, including 10% off sports clothing and 15% off our entire range of kitchen appliances, including fridges. But the biggest savings today can be found in our footwear department, where we have an incredible 50% off all casual shoes. Don\'t miss out on these unmatched reductions!',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','54e574ab-9cd6-44b5-aad4-0f2ab3987533','set2'),(564,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to the announcement about a new shop. Who is the new shop for?\nThe new shop is for people who like ________________.\n','Announcer: Opening this Friday on Elm Street: \'Grand Elegance\'. If you are searching for cheap deals or looking to buy everyday grocery food, this might not be the place for you. However, if you appreciate the finer things in life, from designer watches to high-end silk scarves, our doors are open. Come to \'Grand Elegance\'—the ultimate destination for lovers of luxury items.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','189fe65f-9542-45a2-bd61-6e34c99644df','set2'),(565,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Four people are talking about their weekends.\nComplete the sentences below.\n','Speaker A: On Saturdays, I like to wake up early and get all my grocery shopping, cleaning, and laundry out of the way by noon. Once everything is done, I can completely unwind and do absolutely nothing for the rest of the weekend.\n\nSpeaker B: I don\'t like sitting around on weekends; it bores me. To truly recharge my batteries, I need to stay active. I spend my Saturdays gardening, painting the house, or doing DIY projects. For me, keeping busy is how I relax.\n\nSpeaker C: My weekdays are incredibly hectic, so when Saturday comes, I refuse to rush. I sleep in, read the newspaper in bed, and enjoy a very slow, quiet morning with a cup of coffee before thinking about the rest of the day.\n\nSpeaker D: I work a high-stress job, and my weekends aren\'t any different. I use Saturdays and Sundays to catch up on paperwork, answer emails, and plan for the next week. From the moment I wake up until I go to sleep, I simply don\'t relax during the day.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','5cc6a7fc-c93e-40ab-9100-4e849ffbf73c','set2'),(566,2,'MCQ','a. Speaker A ___________. ',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','5cc6a7fc-c93e-40ab-9100-4e849ffbf73c','set2'),(567,2,'MCQ','b. Speaker B ___________. ',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','5cc6a7fc-c93e-40ab-9100-4e849ffbf73c','set2'),(568,2,'MCQ','c. Speaker C ___________. ',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'click','null','5cc6a7fc-c93e-40ab-9100-4e849ffbf73c','set2'),(569,2,'MCQ','d. Speaker D ___________. ',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'click','null','5cc6a7fc-c93e-40ab-9100-4e849ffbf73c','set2'),(570,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to two people talking about working for companies of different sizes. Read the statements below and decide who expresses which opinion—the man, the woman, or both the man and the woman. Who expresses which opinion?','Man: I\'ve been thinking about applying to a smaller firm. In a massive corporation, your role is so narrowly defined. You just do one specific task every day.\nWoman: That’s very true. In a small company, you get to try everything. However, I worry that promotion chances are much more limited in smaller companies because there are fewer management tiers to climb.\nMan: I agree with you on the promotion limits. But what bothers me about big corporations is how much they invest in structured training opportunities. It\'s a huge benefit that smaller firms can\'t afford.\nWoman: Yes, big companies definitely have the budget for better training. Plus, you can\'t deny the status aspect. When you tell people you work for a world-famous brand, they are always so impressed.\nMan: Absolutely, the prestige of a big name on your CV really does wow people.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','73942431-1e2a-431b-b1d9-4add53644268','set2'),(571,2,'MCQ','Promotion chances are more limited in smaller companies._______.',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','73942431-1e2a-431b-b1d9-4add53644268','set2'),(572,2,'MCQ','Large companies offer more training opportunities. _______',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','73942431-1e2a-431b-b1d9-4add53644268','set2'),(573,2,'MCQ','Large companies have narrowly defined roles for employees________.',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'click','null','73942431-1e2a-431b-b1d9-4add53644268','set2'),(574,2,'MCQ','People are impressed by large companies.________.',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'click','null','73942431-1e2a-431b-b1d9-4add53644268','set2'),(575,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a travel reviewer on the radio talking about a trip and answer the questions below.','Reviewer: Last week, I took a river cruise down the Danube. Now, I usually find cruises to be quite repetitive, but this one offered a surprising mix of historical city tours and nature walks, so it definitely didn\'t lack variety. The cabins and dining areas were top-notch and highly modern, so there were no complaints about inadequate facilities. However, the ship itself felt like a relic from the 1970s—the decor and layout were just far too old-fashioned for my taste.\n\nAs for cruises overall? Many people think they are poor value, but given what is included, I think they are worth the money. They are also skyrocketing in popularity lately. My main critique is that they are highly structured around group dynamics, making them completely unsuitable for individual travellers who prefer independence.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','8655fd6a-cb4a-42cb-9a0d-e315498b7d70','set2'),(576,2,'MCQ','What is the reviewer\'s opinion of the river trip?',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','8655fd6a-cb4a-42cb-9a0d-e315498b7d70','set2'),(577,2,'MCQ','What is the reviewer\'s opinion of cruises overall?',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','8655fd6a-cb4a-42cb-9a0d-e315498b7d70','set2'),(578,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a caterer talking on the radio about catering for large events and answer the questions below.','Caterer: When managing catering for a massive event, people often think the venue\'s visual quality or a massive, varied menu is what matters most. But in my experience, a beautiful hall or fifty different dish choices mean nothing if the food is cold or served late. Appropriate scheduling is the absolute key to good catering; timing is everything.\n\nLooking at the catering industry in general, customers often complain that it’s hard to find a truly reliable caterer, but there are plenty of good ones out there if you look. Many people assume the best firms always specialize in one type of cuisine, but I disagree. The top agencies are usually the ones versatile enough to handle anything from weddings to corporate gigs.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','e66c7d56-fc6d-47af-aa9f-ae4d56612cd7','set2'),(579,2,'MCQ','What does the man think is the most important thing at large events?',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','e66c7d56-fc6d-47af-aa9f-ae4d56612cd7','set2'),(580,2,'MCQ','What is the man\'s opinion about catering in general?',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','e66c7d56-fc6d-47af-aa9f-ae4d56612cd7','set2'),(581,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Sarah is calling her brother. Why does she say she will be late?\r\nSarah is late because she is ____________.','Sarah: Ty, it\'s me. Don\'t wait up for dinner. My afternoon meeting actually wrapped up early, and the roads are completely clear, so traffic isn\'t an issue. But my appointment at the medical clinic got pushed back, and I\'m still sitting here waiting to see the doctor. I\'ll head over as soon as I\'m done.',NULL,2,0,NULL,'click','null','68eafc3e-55c5-4a74-b3b1-6c0a79c6ed53','set3'),(582,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','The friends are deciding where to eat tonight. Where do they agree to go?\r\nThey decide to go to the ____________.','Friend A: What are you craving for dinner? I know that new Italian place just opened up down the road.\r\nFriend B: I had pasta for lunch, actually. How about getting some sushi instead?\r\nFriend A: I\'m not a huge fan of raw fish. Can we just grab some gourmet burgers and fries at the place on the corner?\r\nFriend B: Yeah, alright, that works for me. Let\'s do that.',NULL,2,0,NULL,'click','null','6fcf91df-3efc-4ca5-9e18-abaef9613cbc','set3'),(583,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Liam leaves a message about his holiday booking. What type of accommodation did he choose?\nLiam booked a ____________.','Liam: Hi Mum! Just updating you on my trip next month. I looked into booking a hotel room, but it was far too expensive. Then I considered staying at a campsite to save money, but the weather forecast looks terrible. In the end, I found a lovely, fully furnished holiday apartment online. It has its own kitchen and is right by the beach!',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','9aeb3d4b-006f-4b17-a613-18df0f9b0ce4','set3'),(584,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a father talking to his daughter. What does he want her to do today?\nHe wants her to ____________.','Father: Emma, before you go out with your friends today, please make sure your chores are done. I already took care of watering the plants in the garden, and we can take the car to the automated wash tomorrow. However, your bedroom is an absolute mess with clothes all over the floor, so please tidy it up before you leave.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','06c3756e-baf6-427d-8a62-b16f5dc7d6a9','set3'),(585,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','A courier leaves a voicemail about a package. When will the package arrive?\nThe package will be delivered on ____________.','Courier: Hello, this is a delivery notification for parcel 402. We initially scheduled your delivery for Tuesday morning, but there was a delay at our main warehouse. We managed to get it on the truck today, Wednesday, but we won\'t reach your zone until tomorrow morning. Please ensure someone is home on Thursday to sign for it.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','c5c28a58-f176-4e33-bf68-0f50ebf28794','set3'),(586,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Two colleagues are discussing their weekend plans. What is the man going to do?\nThe man is going to ____________.','Woman: Any plans for the weekend, Dave? I\'m going to see that new science fiction movie at the cinema.\nMan: Nice! I wanted to check out the new art exhibition at the museum, but tickets sold out. Instead, I managed to grab a last-minute ticket to see my favourite rock band play live at the stadium. I can\'t wait for the show!',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','7ef4c2dd-43ef-49dd-91e8-b78084c82acb','set3'),(587,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a woman talking to a receptionist at a gym. What did she leave behind?\nThe woman lost her ____________.','Customer: Excuse me, I was working out in the weight room earlier and I think I left something behind. I checked my bag and I have my water bottle and my locker key right here. However, I can\'t find my blue track jacket anywhere. It\'s chilly outside, so I really need it. Has anyone turned it in?',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','1cbe5ed5-ea37-4df2-9291-63e12612cb0a','set3'),(588,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to two workers talking in an office. What is the problem?\nThe office is too ____________.','Worker A: Do you mind if I turn on this desk lamp? The natural light from the window isn\'t quite enough today.\nWorker B: Go ahead. Hey, is it just me, or is the air conditioning blasting way too high?\nWorker A: No, you\'re right. It\'s absolutely freezing in here today. I can barely type! Let\'s go see if we can find the thermostat.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','992423e0-e558-46b2-a58d-bace665f93a6','set3'),(589,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a student talking about her language studies. Which language does she find most difficult?\nThe student struggles most with ____________.','Student: I\'ve been studying three languages this semester. Spanish has been quite smooth because the grammar rules are very straightforward. I thought French pronunciation would trip me up, but I\'ve actually gotten the hang of it quite well. German, on the other hand, is a nightmare. The sentence structure and word endings are just so complicated for me.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','4a8324a3-d932-47d1-b989-898d95b8a33a','set3'),(590,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to the radio weather announcement. What will the weather be like on Sunday?\nOn Sunday, it will be ____________.','Weather Presenter: Looking at our weekend outlook, Friday\'s heavy rain will clear up by tomorrow morning, giving way to a very gusty and windy Saturday. Make sure to hold onto your hats! Fortunately, the winds will die down by the time we reach Sunday, leaving us with a beautiful, clear, and completely sunny day perfect for a picnic.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','f15acbea-5284-4552-84d2-e6d821c6c271','set3'),(591,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to an airport announcement. Why is Flight BA204 delayed?\r\nThe flight is delayed due to ____________.','Announcer: Passenger announcement for Flight BA204 to Paris. The aircraft is mechanically sound, so there are no technical faults today, and the clear skies mean the weather is perfect for flying. However, due to severe congestion and delays with air traffic control over European airspace, your departure time has been pushed back by one hour.',NULL,2,0,NULL,'click','null','87e1c6c4-3f18-4e33-b9bc-2e3e7c75796b','set3'),(592,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a customer in a bookstore. What kind of book is he looking for?\nThe customer wants to buy a ____________ book.','Customer: Hi, I\'m looking for a gift for my father. He usually reads historical biographies, but his bookshelf is completely full of them. He\'s planning a trip to Italy next summer, so I thought about getting him a travel guide, but my mum already bought him one. Do you have any recommendations in your science fiction section? He\'s recently taken an interest in space stories.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','7e33a89b-cd7b-4aaa-92d3-f9a6ea29dbe2','set3'),(593,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to an announcement on a train platform. Where is the train terminating?\nThe final destination of this train is ____________.','Announcer: The train approaching platform 3 is the 14:15 service to London Waterloo. Please note that due to engineering works on the line, this train will no longer call at Bristol Temple Meads. It will run directly to Bath Spa, where the service will terminate. Passengers for London must disembark at Bath and catch the replacement bus service.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','a66b654b-d212-4243-9041-e004f16c7cad','set3'),(594,6,'MCQ','The bar graph given below shows the average scores of men and women across five groups',NULL,'uploads/questions/q-5da9ed71-63a9-4063-a634-3f1e360bf7a6.png',1,0,NULL,'click','null','cb62c340-93df-489e-8584-8894fd6a84c8','set1'),(595,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a radio advert for a museum. What is the new exhibition about?\nThe new exhibition features ____________.','Voiceover: Experience history like never before at the City Museum. While our famous display of ancient Roman coins remains open to the public, this weekend marks the launch of our brand-new gallery. Come walk through a breathtaking collection of vintage black-and-white photographs capturing city life in the early 1900s. Please note our modern sculpture garden is currently closed for renovations.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','fc6219c9-0073-4d06-a70d-efd64decfb29','set3'),(596,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Four people are talking about how they start their day. Complete the sentences below.','Speaker A: The very first thing I do when my alarm goes off is grab my smartphone off the nightstand. Before I even get out of bed, I open my inbox and check all my work emails to see what kind of day I have ahead of me.\n\nSpeaker B: I can\'t start my day without some fresh air and movement. As soon as I wake up, I lace up my trainers and head out the door for a brisk five-kilometre run. I only sit down to eat my breakfast once I\'ve showered and stretched.\n\nSpeaker C: I love a slow morning routine. I turn on the electric kettle to make a mug of herbal tea because coffee makes me too jittery. Then, I sit at the kitchen table and read a few chapters of a physical fiction novel while I eat my toast.\n\nSpeaker D: My kitchen is always full of sound in the morning. While I\'m pouring my cereal and making my morning espresso, I always have the kitchen radio turned up loud so I can catch up on world news and traffic reports before my commute.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','a4df9b2b-25c0-4d5c-809f-b373402f5c61','set3'),(597,2,'MCQ','Speaker A: __________________',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','a4df9b2b-25c0-4d5c-809f-b373402f5c61','set3'),(598,2,'MCQ','Speaker B: __________________',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','a4df9b2b-25c0-4d5c-809f-b373402f5c61','set3'),(599,2,'MCQ','Speaker C: __________________',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'click','null','a4df9b2b-25c0-4d5c-809f-b373402f5c61','set3'),(600,2,'MCQ','Speaker D: __________________',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'click','null','a4df9b2b-25c0-4d5c-809f-b373402f5c61','set3'),(601,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a conversation between a man and a woman discussing working from home. Decide who expresses each opinion—the man, the woman, or both.','Man: I\'ve been working from home for six months now, and my bank account looks great. Not having to buy a monthly train pass or pay for petrol saves a fortune.\nWoman: That’s definitely true, the savings on commuting are massive. But I find that trying to brainstorm or collaborate on creative projects via video calls is just incredibly clunky and difficult compared to being in the same room.\nMan: Really? I think online collaboration tools work fine. My issue is more emotional; I miss the casual office banter and coffee breaks. It gets quite lonely, and you feel really isolated from the team after a while.\nWoman: Oh, I totally agree with you on the social isolation aspect. It\'s easy to feel cut off from everyone. However, my biggest hurdle is just my environment. Between the laundry, the television, and the fridge, there are too many distractions at home to maintain focus.\nMan: I don\'t have that issue. I actually find my house quieter than a noisy open-plan office, so focus isn\'t a problem for me.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','1ad80e52-e0ea-4dc5-b81a-e0181e8b0888','set3'),(602,2,'MCQ','Working from home saves a significant amount of money on transport. _______',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','1ad80e52-e0ea-4dc5-b81a-e0181e8b0888','set3'),(603,2,'MCQ','It is much harder to collaborate on projects when working remotely. _______',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','1ad80e52-e0ea-4dc5-b81a-e0181e8b0888','set3'),(604,2,'MCQ','Remote work can lead to a feeling of social isolation from colleagues. _______',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'click','null','1ad80e52-e0ea-4dc5-b81a-e0181e8b0888','set3'),(605,2,'MCQ','Distractions at home make it difficult to stay focused all day. _______',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'click','null','1ad80e52-e0ea-4dc5-b81a-e0181e8b0888','set3'),(606,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to an environmentalist talking on the radio about renewable energy developments.','Speaker: Solar energy technology has come an incredibly long way. The public interest is clearly there, and manufacturing costs have plummeted, making panels highly affordable. The real hurdle we face right now isn\'t generating the power—it\'s storing it. Our current battery and energy storage technology is simply inadequate to keep power held for days when the sun isn\'t shining.\n\nWhen we look at wind energy, there is always a fierce debate. Some critics worry about wind farms damaging local bird wildlife, but studies show the impact is minimal when managed correctly. What we really need to focus on is placement. Building wind farms out at sea—offshore—is far superior to onshore setups because ocean winds are much stronger and more consistent, and they don\'t interfere with communities.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','7f0f52f5-5c67-45f6-b25d-58c94bb27504','set3'),(607,2,'MCQ','What does the speaker think is the main barrier to switching to solar energy?',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','7f0f52f5-5c67-45f6-b25d-58c94bb27504','set3'),(608,2,'MCQ','What is the speaker\'s opinion about wind farms in general?',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','7f0f52f5-5c67-45f6-b25d-58c94bb27504','set3'),(610,5,'MCQ','Yesterday afternoon, I bought ____________ new book.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','18038c72-4025-473e-839b-73363d80b6dd','set2'),(611,5,'MCQ','There are _____________ chairs available in the conference room.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','554dfae3-d1d9-43af-a409-2257023af786','set2'),(612,5,'MCQ','This assignment is much easier _________ the last one.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','4d9b44e2-330a-4fd7-bd29-93edacf9170e','set2'),(613,5,'MCQ','I ________ like listening to instrumental music while studying.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','37adedc0-2ed3-4b63-85e6-8358c0fc9e5b','set2'),(614,5,'MCQ','They __________ to go on a trip around Europe next month.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','65e1c1db-7562-4ed4-9b0a-cca212b74167','set2'),(615,5,'MCQ','If the weather __________ clear tonight, we will see the stars.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','e44ed8b1-ebef-4acb-a3a5-e6961ab45de6','set2'),(616,5,'MCQ','The audience was completely __________ by his amazing performance.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','472931d6-8f1c-4218-85c3-8a2a2bd52c67','set2'),(617,5,'MCQ','He doesn\'t ___________ wake up early on Sundays.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','096d6082-c183-48d6-b003-2ec53c9943f5','set2'),(618,5,'MCQ','Have you ever ___________ an authentic Italian pizza before?',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','0a67a8c9-c618-4188-ab63-23e8a001a607','set2'),(619,5,'MCQ',' I ___________ leave now to catch my flight.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','5128c0e1-cb6b-49ca-95b7-1e450352e411','set2'),(620,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','David calls his coworker to explain why he is late for his shift. Why is David late?\n\nDavid is late because ____________.','David: Hi Rachel, it\'s David. I\'m so sorry, but I\'m going to be about half an hour late for our morning shift. I woke up right on time because my alarm was blasting, so that\'s not the issue. I thought about taking the subway, but the train lines are completely shut down for maintenance today anyway. Unfortunately, my car engine just cut out completely on the highway and I\'m currently waiting for a tow truck.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','9eeff782-5d20-4da1-af51-ca8aa964a975','set4'),(621,5,'MCQ','The team managed ___________ the game despite the heavy rain.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','8c8d656c-fd97-41b0-bb68-0e677673078b','set2'),(622,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a family discussing their weekend plans. Where do they agree to go?\n\nThe family decides to visit the ____________.','Father: Alright kids, what are we doing this Saturday? We could go see the monkeys at the zoo.\n\nDaughter: Oh, we went there last month. Can we go to the theme park instead and ride the rollercoasters?\n\nMother: Tickets for the theme park are too expensive this weekend. Why don\'t we check out that new space exploration exhibit at the science museum? Entry is half-price.\n\nDaughter: Okay, that actually sounds really cool. Let\'s do that!',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','f2e628e0-84ac-4f0b-ae10-8e7d213222e2','set4'),(624,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','A tenant calls his landlord to report an issue. What is the main problem with the apartment?\n\nThe tenant is complaining about a broken ____________.','Tenant: Hello Mr. Green, it\'s Tom from flat 4B. I\'m just calling about a few maintenance issues. The kitchen window that was stuck last week is opening fine now, and the fridge is keeping the food perfectly cold, so those are okay. However, the central heater has completely stopped working this morning. The flat is absolutely freezing, and I really need someone to come fix it today.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','5ef67ea0-6e04-4d87-b2e5-2dd14e2ad4cc','set4'),(625,5,'MCQ','_______________ were you chatting with at the market?',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','a22662c7-849a-4fbc-8b01-f9e86254c8ea','set2'),(626,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a student talking to a university advisor. What subject does she decide to study?\n\nThe student signs up for the ____________ course.','Advisor: Welcome! Let\'s look at your elective options for this term. We have a great sociology course, though the reading list is quite long. There is also an introductory economics class if you want to understand global markets.\n\nStudent: I\'m not great with numbers, so economics might be too tricky. I was actually hoping to take a class on human behavior and how the mind works. Is there any space left in the psychology course?\n\nAdvisor: Yes, we just had a slot open up this morning. I\'ll register you for that right now.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','6b71de76-7054-4a1b-a628-c067a1ebb152','set4'),(627,5,'MCQ','There were ___________ people at the gallery than last weekend.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','54e7f1ba-a852-4e92-b8c2-898152905ab6','set2'),(628,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to an office receptionist talking to a delivery driver. What item has arrived?\n\nThe driver has delivered the new ____________.','Receptionist: Hi there! Are those the new ergonomic office chairs we ordered?\n\nDriver: No, those are scheduled for delivery next Tuesday. I have a large box of printer paper here, but that\'s for the accounting office next door. For your office, I just have this express box containing the premium espresso coffee machine you requested for the staff kitchen.\n\nReceptionist: Fantastic! We\'ve been desperate for a good cup of coffee. Sign me up.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','25854265-085d-4eda-b142-65463c61e414','set4'),(629,5,'MCQ','I saw a beautiful bird inside _____________ on my way home.\r\n\r\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','3f2954b0-39ef-486b-bdfd-85e22f11b5fa','set2'),(630,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a teenager talking to his friend about his new part-time job. What does he do?\n\nThe boy works as a ____________.','Boy: I started my new weekend job yesterday!\n\nGirl: Oh nice! Are you still working at that café as a waiter?\n\nBoy: No, the hours were too long. I thought about applying for a dog walker position in the neighborhood, but the pay wasn\'t great. Instead, I\'m working with my uncle helping him landscape backyards. Being a gardener is hard work, but I love being outside in the sun.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','74483d18-f7e7-4f55-be0d-e3289c135336','set4'),(631,5,'MCQ','She prefers tea, __________ her husband always drinks dark coffee.\r\nA. indeed      B. despite      C. whereas\r\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','8c2751e5-3ca8-42f9-ad7c-4ea10f856868','set2'),(632,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','A woman is shopping for a housewarming gift for her friend. What does she buy?\r\n\r\nThe woman buys a ____________.','Customer: Hi, I\'m looking for a nice housewarming present for a friend who just bought a flat. I saw some beautiful ceramic mugs, but she already has a cupboard full of them. She loves baking, so I considered a gourmet cookbook, but she gets all her recipes online anyway. I think I\'ll go with this lovely indoor cheese plant instead. It will look perfect in her new living room.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','3540ff61-f009-423d-8367-3a51ae41181b','set4'),(633,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to an announcement at an airport gate. Why is Flight terminal gate changing?\n\nThe gate change is due to ____________.','Announcer: Attention all passengers for Flight BA332 to Rome. The weather along our flight path is completely clear, so there are no storm delays today. Additionally, all passengers have cleared security checks ahead of schedule. However, due to an extended deep-cleaning delay on the aircraft currently at Gate 14, our departure gate has been moved to Gate 22. Please proceed there immediately.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','2d29bf4c-06cb-4924-95e9-e894272abed0','set4'),(634,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a woman talking to a gym receptionist. Which membership plan does she choose?\n\nThe woman signs up for the ____________ plan.','Receptionist: We have a few different options. Our Weekend Only plan is great if you work Mon-Fri, and our Full Access Monthly card lets you come 24/7, though it is our most expensive option.\n\nCustomer: I work night shifts, so I never come in the evenings or weekends anyway. I just want to use the pool and treadmills on Tuesday and Thursday mornings. The Off-Peak Daytime plan sounds like it fits my schedule perfectly and saves me money. Let\'s go with that.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','ae4647b4-e926-4889-8204-f4809ae53b66','set4'),(635,5,'MCQ','If you had checked the map, we wouldn\'t be lost, _________ we?\r\n\r\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','9ff04f08-a000-4e39-a97c-4ae6cf987e67','set2'),(636,5,'MCQ','We would ___________ the deadline if we had worked together.\r\n\r\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','1d4e2bca-ec30-4ee8-9e7e-efff39f6a36e','set2'),(637,5,'MCQ',' I _______________ living in this city now for over ten years.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','c9ff04ba-2dc6-4d49-9a7b-7bdf6088d6eb','set2'),(638,5,'MCQ','He is believed _____________ the oldest citizen in the town.\n\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','0b6ca201-6f19-4047-bd55-af6710d30806','set2'),(639,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a radio book review. What genre is the reviewer\'s favorite book of the month?\n\nThe reviewer\'s top book recommendation is a ____________.','Reviewer: I\'ve read some fantastic titles this month. The new historical biography of Winston Churchill was incredibly detailed, though a bit slow at times. I also dived into a space-travel science fiction novel, which had a great concept but flat characters. But my absolute standout favorite was a gripping mystery thriller set in an isolated Scottish village. The plot twists kept me guessing until the final page. You must buy it!',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','37a73f30-a7b1-4598-8f35-97a96fdec6ba','set4'),(640,5,'MCQ','The book, ___________ was published in 1920, became a bestseller.\n\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','077430a7-2062-49ef-b700-2ebb30f84e06','set2'),(641,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to an announcement on a commuter train. What item has been found?\n\nSomeone left a ____________ on the train.','Conductor: Good afternoon, passengers. A quick lost property update. A black laptop bag found under a seat in Carriage C has already been returned to its rightful owner. We also had a set of house keys handed in, but they belong to a staff member. However, a blue checkered umbrella was just found left behind on the luggage rack in Carriage E. If this is yours, please see the attendant at the next station.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','db3d34e9-01c4-432d-8c9b-4fe99c013eb3','set4'),(642,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a man telling a story to his friend. What did he ruin while cooking dinner?\n\nThe man accidentally ruined the ____________.','Speaker: I tried to cook a fancy three-course meal last night and it was a disaster. The tomato soup appetizer turned out delicious, and the chocolate cake I baked for dessert was absolutely perfect. But while I was distracted checking on the cake, I completely forgot about the main course on the stove. I left the ribeye steaks cooking for way too long and they ended up completely burnt to a crisp! We had to order pizza.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','1145baea-61d3-4271-81bf-3e399fc87c80','set4'),(643,5,'MCQ','By next Sunday evening, we will ________________ our exams.\r\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','b631a640-d2d4-4ba2-b74d-340c79baea4d','set2'),(644,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to an announcement at a library. Where is the evening poetry reading taking place?\r\n\r\nThe event will be held in the ____________.','Announcer: Good evening, visitors. Please note that our main reading room will close 30 minutes early tonight at 6:30 pm to prepare for cleaning. If you are here for the guest poetry reading event tonight, please note that it will not take place in the basement auditorium as originally advertised. Due to the beautiful weather, the event has been moved up to the rooftop garden on the fourth floor. Enjoy the evening!',NULL,4,0,NULL,'click','null','fdc4862a-423f-43e7-bbfe-7e149e404017','set4'),(645,5,'MCQ','You ____________me about the cancellation before I drove all the way here!\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','4534d041-5c1c-4857-ad6d-4ca5c67ce09d','set2'),(646,5,'MCQ','If I had practiced harder last winter, I wouldn\'t _____________ struggle now.\n\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','ca9695f9-8006-456b-b506-1de6dcca7b0e','set2'),(647,5,'MCQ','He told us he loved reading and that he ____________ that novel twice.\n\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','78f5d15b-a9e6-4bf4-878f-cacd3895a8ed','set2'),(648,5,'MCQ','It\'s freezing outside. If only I___________ a warm jacket with me.\n\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','e4d34353-f1f0-4317-8495-961677c0141d','set2'),(649,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Four people are describing how they stay productive in the morning. Match Speaker A-D to options 1-6.','Speaker A: If I don\'t organize my thoughts right away, my day becomes chaotic. While I\'m eating my oatmeal and drinking my coffee, I always sit down with a notebook and map out a strict, written to-do list of everything I need to accomplish by 5 pm.\n\n\nSpeaker B: I don\'t care about emails or food when I first wake up. To get my brain working, I need movement. I change straight into my fitness gear, head down to my basement gym, and complete a heavy 45-minute weight or cardio workout on an empty stomach.\n\n\nSpeaker C: My morning rule is absolute calm. Before turning on any screens or looking at a phone, I sit cross-legged on the living room floor, close my eyes, and spend ten minutes focusing entirely on my breathing in total silence. It stops me from feeling stressed.\n\nSpeaker D: I have a bad habit of reaching for my phone the millisecond my eyes open. Before my feet even touch the carpet, I spend about fifteen minutes scrolling through news feeds and checking social media notifications to see what happened overnight.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','a2a56612-8145-45be-8d5b-0b590242a439','set4'),(650,2,'MCQ','a. Speaker A: ____',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','a2a56612-8145-45be-8d5b-0b590242a439','set4'),(651,2,'MCQ','b. Speaker B: ____',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','a2a56612-8145-45be-8d5b-0b590242a439','set4'),(652,2,'MCQ','c. Speaker C: ____',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'click','null','a2a56612-8145-45be-8d5b-0b590242a439','set4'),(653,2,'MCQ','d. Speaker D: ____',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'click','null','a2a56612-8145-45be-8d5b-0b590242a439','set4'),(654,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a discussion between a student (man) and a guidance counselor (woman) about higher education paths. Decide who expresses each opinion—the man, the woman, or both.','Man: I\'m trying to decide between going to a traditional four-year university or enrolling in a technical trade school to become an electrician.\n\nWoman: Well, they both have massive benefits. Moving away to a university campus is an incredible experience for building personal independence and learning how to look after yourself.\n\nMan: That\'s true, the life experience at university is great. But trade school is only two years long, meaning those practical courses let you graduate and enter the workforce much faster than a standard degree path.\n\nWoman: Oh, absolutely, the speed of getting into a job is a huge plus for trade schools. And let’s be honest, the job market has changed. Having a standard university degree simply doesn\'t guarantee a high-paying corporate position anymore like it used to.\n\nMan: I completely agree. So many of my graduated friends are working retail jobs. That\'s why learning a technical trade is so appealing right now; specialized skills are in high demand, which can lead to incredible financial security and steady income.\n\nWoman: Definitely. Plumbers and electricians are always needed, so you\'ll never be short of work or money.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','99667551-cad9-4bcc-a058-922a9beea870','set4'),(655,2,'MCQ','Traditional universities provide a great environment for personal independence. ____',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','99667551-cad9-4bcc-a058-922a9beea870','set4'),(656,2,'MCQ','Trade school courses allow students to enter the workforce much faster. ____',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','99667551-cad9-4bcc-a058-922a9beea870','set4'),(657,2,'MCQ','A university degree no longer guarantees a high-paying corporate job. ____',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'click','null','99667551-cad9-4bcc-a058-922a9beea870','set4'),(658,2,'MCQ','Learning a technical trade can lead to excellent financial security. ____',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'click','null','99667551-cad9-4bcc-a058-922a9beea870','set4'),(659,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to an agricultural scientist talking on the radio about food production trends.','Agronomist: Vertical farming inside automated indoor warehouses is completely changing agriculture. While the initial setup is expensive and the vegetables don\'t grow any larger than farm-grown ones, the environmental savings are massive. Because vertical farms recycle moisture through closed-loop hydroponic systems, they require up to ninety-five percent less water than traditional soil farming. It\'s a game-changer for drought-prone regions.\n\nHowever, outside of indoor facilities, traditional farming still relies heavily on chemical intervention. Everyone worries about pesticide traces on their grocery store apples, but the real ecological crisis is beneath our feet. Excessive pesticide run-off from massive fields is seeping into the soil and permanently contaminating deep freshwater resources and rivers, creating long-term environmental hazards that are incredibly difficult to reverse.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','91635e79-88d7-430e-ac51-1f7e9420e04b','set4'),(660,2,'MCQ','What does the speaker identify as the primary advantage of indoor vertical farming?',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','91635e79-88d7-430e-ac51-1f7e9420e04b','set4'),(661,2,'MCQ','What is the speaker\'s warning regarding global pesticide use?',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','91635e79-88d7-430e-ac51-1f7e9420e04b','set4'),(662,5,'QUESTION_FORM','Select a word from each drop-down list on the right that has the same or a very similar meaning to each word on the left. Use each word once only.',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,'click','null','bfdda76b-3c05-4db3-a4c0-3650693809ab','set1'),(663,5,'MCQ','modify',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'select','null','bfdda76b-3c05-4db3-a4c0-3650693809ab','set2'),(664,5,'MCQ','buy',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'select','null','bfdda76b-3c05-4db3-a4c0-3650693809ab','set2'),(665,5,'MCQ','reduce',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'select','null','bfdda76b-3c05-4db3-a4c0-3650693809ab','set2'),(666,5,'MCQ','abandon',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'select','null','bfdda76b-3c05-4db3-a4c0-3650693809ab','set2'),(667,5,'MCQ','keep',NULL,NULL,1,5,NULL,'select','null','bfdda76b-3c05-4db3-a4c0-3650693809ab','set2'),(668,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Chloe calls her classmate to ask for help. What did Chloe forget to bring home?\nChloe forgot her ____________.','Chloe: Hi Marcus, it\'s Chloe. I\'m just calling to see if you are still at school. I have my school bag with me, and I checked inside and my history textbook is right here. But I\'ve just realized I left my locker key sitting on my desk in the homeroom. I can\'t get to any of my revision notes for tomorrow\'s test unless someone can grab it for me!',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','1f6107c9-902f-46de-92d8-281e793c3758','set5'),(669,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to two friends organizing a day out. What do they decide to do?\n\nThe friends agree to ____________.','Friend A: Hey, the weather is supposed to be beautiful tomorrow. Shall we go to that new contemporary art gallery downtown?\n\nFriend B: Oh, I spent all of last weekend indoors. I\'d rather do something outside. What about wandering around the big botanical garden?\n\nFriend A: I went there with my parents on Tuesday, actually. Why don\'t we check out the seasonal outdoor market by the river? There\'s live music and street food stalls.\n\nFriend B: Oh, fantastic idea! Let\'s do that instead.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','d85afd0b-8e9d-4a8d-85be-1ab12b8357da','set5'),(670,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','A woman calls a local community center. What evening course does she register for?\n\nThe woman signs up for a ____________ class.','Customer: Hi, I\'m calling to book a spot in one of your evening courses starting next week. I originally wanted to join the creative writing group, but it clashes with my work hours. I also looked at the woodworking workshop, but it requires buying a lot of expensive tools beforehand. Is there still space left in the Tuesday night beginners\' yoga session?\n\nReceptionist: Yes, we have two slots left. I\'ll get your name down for that right away.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','73d45f04-b8d7-42d2-9871-5eca924c3784','set5'),(671,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a customer service agent talking to a client. Why is the package delayed?\n\nThe delivery is late because of ____________.','Agent: Hello Mr. Vance, I\'m calling regarding your delayed parcel. We verified the shipping address on the box and it matches your details perfectly, so that wasn\'t the issue. The delivery van did experience a mechanical failure this morning, but a replacement vehicle was sent immediately. The real issue is that the international sender forgot to attach a vital customs clearance document, so the airport facility won\'t release it to us until that\'s sorted.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','6ab2fe46-3269-47e3-8a56-a1f7f9114ba1','set5'),(672,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','A man leaves a message for his family about their holiday accommodation. What did he choose?\n\nThe man booked a ____________.','Speaker: Hi everyone, great news about our trip next month! I spent hours browsing options online. I looked at some high-end luxury hotel rooms, but they didn\'t have a common area for us to sit together. Then I found a beautiful beachside apartment, but it was far too noisy. In the end, I found a lovely, quiet traditional cottage nestled in the valley. It has plenty of space and a massive fireplace!',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','3c1c02b3-1fb2-4047-94c8-d067e4cff38c','set5'),(673,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a teacher giving instructions to his students. What must they hand in before Friday?\n\nStudents need to submit their ____________.','Teacher: Listen up, class. Regarding our field trip to the science museum next Tuesday: I\'ve already received medical forms from everyone, so thank you. Please remember your science projects aren\'t due until the end of term, so don\'t worry about those yet. However, I am still missing the signed parental permission slips from half of you. If you don\'t bring that slip to my desk by Friday morning, you won\'t be allowed on the bus.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','822ba457-e971-4023-8de9-f035c5df292a','set5'),(674,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to an announcement at a shopping mall information desk. What item has been handed in?\n\nSomeone has found a lost ____________.','Announcer: Good afternoon, shoppers. A quick notice from customer services. A smartphone found on the second floor near the food court has now been successfully returned to its owner. We\'ve also had a shopper report a missing bunch of house keys, which we are still looking for. However, a black leather wallet containing a bus pass was just handed in by a security guard. Please come to the ground-floor desk to claim it.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','1e1a3868-acb4-4b2e-b747-6b8cb224d872','set5'),(675,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a woman talking about her recent trip abroad. What gift did she bring back for her dad?\n\nThe woman bought her father a ____________.','Speaker: I had a fantastic time visiting the mountains in Switzerland. Shopping for souvenirs was tricky, though. I thought about buying a box of their famous local chocolates, but my dad is on a strict low-sugar diet. I also saw some beautifully crafted leather belts, but they were incredibly expensive. In the end, I stopped by a local farm and picked up a jar of organic regional honey. He absolute loves it on his morning toast.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','a36b8dd3-b11d-49f5-8bae-7504efb288d5','set5'),(676,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a radio announcement about a sporting event. Why was the match cancelled?\n\nThe football match was called off because of ____________.','Presenter: We have some disappointing news for sports fans tuning in today. This evening\'s highly anticipated football derby at the stadium has been officially postponed. The rumors that several key team members were out with sudden illnesses have been denied by the club manager. While the heavy rain did cause some minor waterlogging on the pitch, ground staff managed to drain it completely. The real issue is a major malfunction in the stadium\'s local power grid, which has left the massive floodlights completely unusable.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','99e9ca7e-9525-42ac-a999-60af0d83cdae','set5'),(677,5,'QUESTION_FORM','Complete each definition using a word from the drop-down list. Use each word once only.',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,'select','null','44acd62e-6028-477f-9e59-07fb5462548f','set2'),(678,5,'MCQ','The paramedic drove the ____________ quickly to the clinic.',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'select','null','44acd62e-6028-477f-9e59-07fb5462548f','set2'),(679,5,'MCQ','The travel agency handles every single ____________ with care.',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'select','null','44acd62e-6028-477f-9e59-07fb5462548f','set2'),(680,5,'MCQ','A professional ____________ repaired our vehicle engine.',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'select','null','44acd62e-6028-477f-9e59-07fb5462548f','set2'),(681,5,'MCQ','She carried a small piece of hand ____________ onto the flight',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'select','null','44acd62e-6028-477f-9e59-07fb5462548f','set2'),(682,5,'MCQ','We stayed next to a beautiful historical piece of ____________.',NULL,NULL,1,5,NULL,'select','null','44acd62e-6028-477f-9e59-07fb5462548f','set2'),(683,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a man talking to a car dealer. What type of vehicle does he choose?\n\nThe customer decides to purchase a ____________ car.','Customer: I\'m having a hard time deciding which model to go for. I drove a petrol-powered car for ten years, but I definitely want something more eco-friendly now. I was very tempted by the fully electric model, but I do a lot of long-distance driving in rural areas where charging points are hard to find. Therefore, I think a hybrid vehicle is the perfect compromise for my current lifestyle—it gives me efficiency without the charging anxiety. Let\'s write up the paperwork.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','b063e63f-514e-40e3-9352-cc5e1377b27e','set5'),(684,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a student talking about her language learning experience. What does she find most difficult?\n\nThe student struggles most with Japanese ____________.','Student: Learning Japanese has been an incredible journey. People warned me that the vocabulary memorization would take months, but I actually find the words quite easy to recall using flashcards. The basic sentence structure is backwards compared to English, but after a few weeks of practice, it starts to feel completely natural. The real hurdle for me is mastering the three distinct writing systems. Memorizing hundreds of complex characters is an absolute nightmare!',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','4fce7e8f-cd8d-4271-bd82-becc4c8d319c','set5'),(685,5,'QUESTION_FORM','Complete each sentence using a word from each drop-down list. Use each word once only. You will not need five of the words.',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,'click','null','3f68590b-d768-4905-8b95-a7d51c6df6c5','set2'),(686,5,'MCQ','Completely calm, serene, and free from any disturbance.',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','3f68590b-d768-4905-8b95-a7d51c6df6c5','set2'),(687,5,'MCQ','Existing or lasting for only a short, limited timeframe.',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'select','null','3f68590b-d768-4905-8b95-a7d51c6df6c5','set2'),(688,5,'MCQ','Very large, heavy, and impressive in size or scale.',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'click','null','3f68590b-d768-4905-8b95-a7d51c6df6c5','set2'),(689,5,'MCQ','Highly precise, correct, and completely free of errors..  ',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'click','null','3f68590b-d768-4905-8b95-a7d51c6df6c5','set2'),(690,5,'MCQ','Showing extreme enthusiasm and desire to do something.',NULL,NULL,1,5,NULL,'click','null','3f68590b-d768-4905-8b95-a7d51c6df6c5','set2'),(691,5,'QUESTION_FORM','Select a word from each drop-down list on the right that has the same or a very similar meaning to each word on the left. Use each word once only. You will not need five of the words.',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,'click','null','0aa784c0-59a3-46c2-bec9-718992a9935e','set2'),(692,5,'MCQ','It is absolutely ____________ that we secure funding now.',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'select','null','0aa784c0-59a3-46c2-bec9-718992a9935e','set2'),(693,5,'MCQ','The work was so repetitive and ____________ that he fell asleep..  ',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'select','null','0aa784c0-59a3-46c2-bec9-718992a9935e','set2'),(694,5,'MCQ','They discovered an ____________ historical manuscript.',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'select','null','0aa784c0-59a3-46c2-bec9-718992a9935e','set2'),(695,5,'MCQ','The system requires an extremely ____________ and strict test.  ',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'select','null','0aa784c0-59a3-46c2-bec9-718992a9935e','set2'),(696,5,'MCQ','The company introduces highly ____________ technological updates.',NULL,NULL,1,5,NULL,'select','null','0aa784c0-59a3-46c2-bec9-718992a9935e','set2'),(697,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Two friends are discussing what to watch on TV. What genre do they pick?\n\nThe friends agree to watch a ____________.','Friend A: Let\'s find something to watch tonight. There\'s a highly rated nature documentary about marine life available to stream.\n\nFriend B: Oh, I\'m too tired for an educational show tonight. I want something thrilling, like a creepy horror film!\n\nFriend A: You know I get terrified easily and won\'t sleep a wink! Can we compromise on a lighthearted romantic comedy? It\'s funny, easy to watch, and we don\'t have to think too much.\n\nFriend B: Fine, okay. As long as there\'s popcorn, I can tolerate a rom-com.',NULL,3,0,NULL,'click','null','20115eec-3d37-416b-bf70-13049bd3667a','set5'),(698,5,'QUESTION_FORM','Select a word from each drop-down list on the right that is most often used with each word on the left.',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,'click','null','3847bb9f-ec37-4c51-af3e-cc5c975c2003','set2'),(699,5,'MCQ','environmental +.  + ',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'select','null','3847bb9f-ec37-4c51-af3e-cc5c975c2003','set2'),(700,5,'MCQ','safety +.  + ',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'select','null','3847bb9f-ec37-4c51-af3e-cc5c975c2003','set2'),(701,5,'MCQ','potential +.  + ',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'select','null','3847bb9f-ec37-4c51-af3e-cc5c975c2003','set2'),(702,5,'MCQ','global +.  + ',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'select','null','3847bb9f-ec37-4c51-af3e-cc5c975c2003','set2'),(703,5,'MCQ','dramatic +.  + ',NULL,NULL,1,5,NULL,'select','null','3847bb9f-ec37-4c51-af3e-cc5c975c2003','set2'),(705,5,'MCQ','Every morning, she enjoys ____________ hot cup of green tea.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','1df9ae12-bf42-4749-8c94-5de34c5339c5','set4'),(706,5,'MCQ','There are _____________ apples left in the kitchen basket.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','bc82dfa4-cf6d-4632-b1f4-9d6e3279c31e','set4'),(707,5,'MCQ','My bedroom is cooler _________ the living room.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','3e420e0e-eb53-494f-8eec-af6db5953230','set4'),(708,5,'MCQ','I ________ dislike waking up early on winter mornings.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','4d837490-e7df-424f-b907-dcb87c30d5e7','set4'),(709,5,'MCQ','We __________ to move into a larger house next spring.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','387cfbb0-59ad-4974-8c16-a99aff3a6507','set4'),(710,5,'MCQ','If it __________ tonight, the roads will become very slippery.',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','4582427b-0685-4582-9aab-725bf4287ea3','set4'),(711,5,'MCQ','The students were utterly __________ by the long lecture.\r\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','99a86175-f2c7-4b4b-a53d-13f855d54a1f','set4'),(712,5,'MCQ','He doesn\'t ___________ visit his relatives during the week.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','4c99e5e9-1ab4-490e-af2e-2b3c59ac977b','set4'),(713,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a diner talking about a restaurant visit. What was the best part of the experience?\r\n\r\nThe diner was most impressed by the ____________.','Speaker: We went to that new French bistro downtown last night. To be completely honest, the menu was incredibly expensive for the portion sizes we received. The interior decoration was also a bit plain and lacked any real warmth or character. However, the customer service was absolutely flawless. The waitstaff were incredibly warm, highly attentive, and anticipated our every need without being intrusive. They made the whole evening special.',NULL,4,0,NULL,'click','null','d1c353b7-7b61-4795-89b8-905eefeec943','set5'),(714,5,'MCQ','Have you ever ___________ to a real classical orchestra?\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','4b9686ff-2efc-48ee-bc69-c24591f221e0','set4'),(715,5,'MCQ','I ___________ complete my homework before going out.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','9a4185a5-daa7-4e5e-bccf-cdb7ce828d05','set4'),(716,5,'MCQ','They managed ___________ the old vehicle after an hour.\r\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','f9712e80-3f4f-4d56-80b4-6365971f5302','set4'),(717,5,'MCQ',' _______________ was driving that red sports car yesterday?\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','62506381-8c00-450a-975a-bc821e38a76e','set4'),(718,5,'MCQ','There was ___________ interest in the project than we hoped.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','5857ff33-b2f0-4dba-96e0-506bc309416a','set4'),(719,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Four professional freelancers describe their ideal working environments. Match Speaker A-D to options 1-6.','Speaker A: I absolutely cannot function if a room is completely quiet; dead silence makes me feel trapped and anxious. I need background energy to stay focused. Every morning, I set up my laptop at a small corner table in a bustling local coffee shop. The hiss of the espresso machine and the low chatter of people around me create the perfect white noise for my writing.\n\nSpeaker B: I am incredibly easily distracted by people, noise, or movement. If a door clicks or someone walks past, my train of thought is instantly ruined. That\'s why I invested in soundproofing for a spare room at the back of my house. I lock myself away in that private home office with noise-canceling headphones, and that total isolation is the only way I get things done.\n\nSpeaker C: Working from home made me feel incredibly isolated and lonely, but coffee shops are too disorganized for me. My solution was to sign up for a monthly membership at a local co-working hub. I get a dedicated professional desk, access to meeting rooms, and most importantly, I\'m surrounded by other independent creators, which makes it feel like a real office community.\n\nSpeaker D: I find sitting at the exact same desk for eight hours completely drains my creativity. To keep my mind sharp, I split my schedule up. I spend my mornings responding to emails at my kitchen table, my afternoons doing creative design work on a bench in the public library, and my evenings wrapping up tasks at a quiet local diner. Constant environmental change keeps me motivated.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','ee7d310f-cac8-465e-9805-a39dfd3504e2','set5'),(720,2,'MCQ','a. Speaker A: ____',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','ee7d310f-cac8-465e-9805-a39dfd3504e2','set5'),(721,2,'MCQ','b. Speaker B: ____',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','ee7d310f-cac8-465e-9805-a39dfd3504e2','set5'),(722,2,'MCQ','c. Speaker C: ____',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'click','null','ee7d310f-cac8-465e-9805-a39dfd3504e2','set5'),(723,2,'MCQ','d. Speaker D: ____',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'click','null','ee7d310f-cac8-465e-9805-a39dfd3504e2','set5'),(724,5,'MCQ','I saw a strange shadow inside _____________ on my way upstairs.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','9c29cda9-8349-47af-a1e2-d1e835fe50a9','set4'),(725,5,'MCQ','The first brother loves math, __________ the second loves art.\r\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','cc73cc89-4726-45aa-83f0-ad8a4ba2f0f8','set4'),(726,5,'MCQ','If you had worn your coat, you wouldn\'t have caught a cold, _________ you?\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','7b3e633a-3ae6-40cb-991a-6ead690630d0','set4'),(727,5,'MCQ','We would ___________ our train if we hadn\'t hurried.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','0d0473a1-04b4-4ec7-84eb-645c41944997','set4'),(728,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a discussion between a traditional book shop owner (man) and an avid digital reader (woman) about the future of reading. Decide who expresses each opinion—the man, the woman, or both.','Man: I see more and more people using digital tablets on their commutes. Do you really think electronic screens are replacing printed paper books completely?\n\nWoman: Honestly, yes. From a practical standpoint, digital e-readers are unmatched for convenience. When I go on holiday, I don\'t have to pack a heavy stack of novels in my suitcase; I can fit an entire library of thousands of titles on one lightweight device.\n\nMan: I can\'t argue with the transport convenience, it\'s definitely useful. But for me, reading isn\'t just about consuming data; it\'s a sensory experience. The weight of the volume, the smell of the ink, and the physical sensation of turning real paper pages create a emotional connection that a cold plastic screen simply cannot replicate.\n\nWoman: I completely understand that nostalgia. However, my biggest complaint with digital reading isn\'t emotional—it\'s physical. After staring at an electronic screen during a long three-hour reading session, my eyes feel incredibly dry and strained.\n\nMan: Exactly! Eye strain is a major drawback of digital devices. That\'s why I firmly believe print isn\'t dying. However, the market will change; printed paper books will eventually stop being cheap, mass-market everyday objects and transform into premium, high-quality collector\'s items for enthusiasts.\n\nWoman: You know, I actually think you\'re right. People will buy digital for convenience and buy print for decoration or collection.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','d9d468c8-2812-437b-a682-15ec72d060ce','set5'),(729,2,'MCQ','Digital e-readers are incredibly convenient for traveling because they hold thousands of titles.',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','d9d468c8-2812-437b-a682-15ec72d060ce','set5'),(730,2,'MCQ','The physical sensation of turning real paper pages cannot be replicated by a screen. ____',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','d9d468c8-2812-437b-a682-15ec72d060ce','set5'),(731,2,'MCQ','Electronic screens can cause significant eye strain during long reading sessions. ____',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'click','null','d9d468c8-2812-437b-a682-15ec72d060ce','set5'),(732,2,'MCQ','Printed paper books will eventually become rare collector\'s items rather than everyday objects. ____',NULL,NULL,1,4,NULL,'click','null','d9d468c8-2812-437b-a682-15ec72d060ce','set5'),(733,5,'MCQ','She _______________ practicing the piano now for over four hours.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','bd3306d1-2a5f-41f4-88f7-7c6640c14333','set4'),(734,5,'MCQ','He is rumored _____________ the secret mastermind of the operation.\nA. to be      B. being      C. been\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','8dee3e63-12bf-46c8-9304-e3add6fd2df2','set4'),(735,2,'AUDIO_MCQ','Listen to a marine conservationist talking on the radio about coral reef tourism.','Biologist: Tourism surrounding coral reefs is a double-edged sword. Critics argue that travel foot traffic causes structural damage to the coral, which can happen. However, we cannot ignore the economic reality. The immense revenue generated by diving tourism doesn\'t just disappear into corporate pockets; it provides vital, direct funding for local marine park rangers and conservation research initiatives that would otherwise have zero financial support.\n\nTo balance tourism with preservation, governments have introduced strict, mandatory wildlife protection zones where all diving, swimming, and boat traffic are completely banned. Some industry groups complain these rules harm business or claim they are impossible to monitor across open water. But the ecological data is undeniable: these completely isolated sanctuaries are incredibly effective, providing a safe haven that allows damaged fish populations and delicate coral structures to regenerate and recover at rapid speeds.',NULL,0,0,NULL,'prompt','null','4c40dd56-d610-49fe-98b4-b8dede8bb20d','set5'),(736,2,'MCQ','What does the speaker say about the financial impact of coral reef diving tourism?',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'click','null','4c40dd56-d610-49fe-98b4-b8dede8bb20d','set5'),(737,2,'MCQ','What is the speaker\'s opinion on mandatory wildlife protection zones?',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'click','null','4c40dd56-d610-49fe-98b4-b8dede8bb20d','set5'),(738,5,'MCQ','The laptop, ___________ was bought last year, is already broken.\nA. which      B. where      C. what\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','a5b94441-2f6e-4367-a16a-35240cee93c7','set4'),(739,5,'MCQ','By this time next winter, they will ________________ their project.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','4b5bd172-a8f7-43ed-a5b1-2d8bc488a176','set4'),(740,5,'MCQ','You ____________me about the road closure before I started driving!\nA. should have told      B. can’t have told      C. must have told\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','31dbe703-58e2-4ab5-9a0c-0907ca2aa562','set4'),(741,5,'MCQ','If I had packed my bag last night, I wouldn\'t _____________ hurrying now.\r\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','6e546b42-3b6b-46a9-ab64-b59e750b3551','set4'),(742,5,'MCQ','She mentioned it was a wonderful film and that she ____________ it before.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','4d136cb6-c61e-4352-8f01-3c93d85a020c','set4'),(743,5,'MCQ','It\'s pouring down. If only I___________ an umbrella with me.\n',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'click','null','c65c03e1-b4c6-4477-9c21-ab3a55f5a147','set4'),(752,5,'QUESTION_FORM','Select a word from each drop-down list on the right that has the same or a very similar meaning to each word on the left. Use each word once only.',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,'click','null','97e9360f-daae-43a7-86f0-7ea56a177fbf','set4'),(753,5,'MCQ','start',NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'select','null','97e9360f-daae-43a7-86f0-7ea56a177fbf','set4'),(754,5,'MCQ','help',NULL,NULL,1,2,NULL,'select','null','97e9360f-daae-43a7-86f0-7ea56a177fbf','set4'),(755,5,'MCQ','finish',NULL,NULL,1,3,NULL,'select','null','97e9360f-daae-43a7-86f0-7ea56a177fbf','set4'),(756,5,'MCQ','ask',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'select','null','97e9360f-daae-43a7-86f0-7ea56a177fbf','set4'),(757,5,'MCQ','gather',NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,'select','null','97e9360f-daae-43a7-86f0-7ea56a177fbf','set4'),(777,5,'QUESTION_FORM','Complete each definition using a word from the drop-down list. Use each word once only.',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,'click','null','0d258565-e774-45d0-a37d-7a710d4c7a8f','set4'),(778,5,'MCQ','Please keep your printed